.TH CARTE\-AGENT 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
carte\-agent \- serve a garnish guest's applications to the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B carte\-agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B carte\-agent
runs in the guest's user session, started by
.BR carte\-agent.service .
It reads the guest's desktop entries, watches them for changes, and serves
the list of applications, their icons and launch requests to
.BR carte (1)
on the host over vsock port 8890. It only accepts connections from CID 2,
the host.
.PP
The VM's name is the guest's hostname, which
.BR gerantd (1)
sets to the name of the VM's configuration.
.SS What is exported
The agent reads
.I applications/
under
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME
and
.BR $XDG_DATA_DIRS ,
subdirectories included; the first file with a given desktop ID wins. It
leaves out entries that are not
.BR Type=Application ,
have
.B NoDisplay
or
.BR Hidden ,
are in the
.B Settings
category, are hidden from GNOME by
.BR OnlyShowIn / NotShowIn ,
have a
.B TryExec
that isn't installed, or have
.BR Terminal=true .
Changes are picked up with inotify, once the directories have been quiet
for a second.
.SS Starting applications
For a launch request, the agent re-reads the desktop entry, applies the same
filter, expands
.B Exec=
(file and URL field codes are dropped), and runs
.PP
.EX
systemd\-run \-\-user \-\-scope \-\-quiet \-\-collect \e
    \-\-unit=app\-carte\-\fIid\fP\-\fIn\fP.scope \-\- \fIargv\fP
.EE
.PP
in
.B Path=
if set, else in the home directory, with the user manager's environment.
That environment needs the Wayland variables; the garnish images set them in
.IR /usr/lib/environment.d/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/carte\-agent.service
Starts the agent in every user's session.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR carte (1),
.BR sonnette\-agent (1),
.BR systemd\-run (1),
.BR garnish (7)
